  data: {
    LLM: "Save your Aces and Kings to specifically use on tricks where you suspect a Jack will be played. If you have a Jack, try to lead it when you've already depleted that suit in your opponents' hands.\n\nBidding Strategy: Only declare a 'Hit' if you have the Jack and the Ace of the same suit. The Ace ensures you can stop anyone from overplaying your lead.\n\nTracking 'Youngs': Keep track of exactly which Jacks have been played. If three are gone, the final Jack becomes the primary target for all players.",
    Player: "Save your Aces and Kings to specifically use on tricks where you suspect a Jack will be played. If you have a Jack, try to lead it when you've already depleted that suit in your opponents' hands.\n\nBidding Strategy: Only declare a 'Hit' if you have the Jack and the Ace of the same suit. The Ace ensures you can stop anyone from overplaying your lead.\n\nTracking 'Youngs': Keep track of exactly which Jacks have been played. If three are gone, the final Jack becomes the primary target for all players.",
